    description: { de: "Eine Küstenstadt in Sinaloa, die als Ausgangspunkt für die Kupfercanyon-Bahn dient.", hu: "Sinaloa tengerparti városa, a Réz-kanyon vasút kiindulópontja.", ro: "Un oraș de coastă din Sinaloa, care servește drept punct de plecare pentru trenul Copper Canyon.", en: "A coastal city in Sinaloa, serving as the starting point for the Copper Canyon railway." },
    facts: { de: ["Wichtiges landwirtschaftliches Zentrum (Zuckerrohr)", "Tor zur Kupferschlucht", "Hafen von Topolobampo in der Nähe"], hu: ["Fontos mezőgazdasági központ (cukornád)", "Kapu a Réz-kanyonhoz", "Topolobampo kikötője a közelben"], ro: ["Centru agricol important (trestie de zahăr)", "Poarta de acces către Canionul de Cupru", "Portul Topolobampo în apropiere"], en: ["Major agricultural center (sugarcane)", "Gateway to the Copper Canyon", "Port of Topolobampo nearby"] },
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Los Mochis ist eine lebhafte Stadt im Bundesstaat Sinaloa und der perfekte Ausgangspunkt für eine Fahrt mit dem berühmten El Chepe-Zug durch die Kupferschlucht. Die Küstenstadt besticht durch ihre breiten Alleen, üppigen botanischen Gärten und eine exzellente Meeresfrüchte-Küche. Hier verschmelzen moderne Urbanität und reiche landwirtschaftliche Traditionen zu einem einzigartigen Charme. Reisende schätzen die Nähe zum Pazifik und die entspannte, authentische Atmosphäre abseits der großen Touristenströme.",
      hu: "",
      ro: "",
      en: "Los Mochis is a modern and prosperous city in northern Sinaloa, serving as the essential western gateway to the world-famous Copper Canyon. Founded by American entrepreneur Benjamin Johnston in the early 20th century as a sugar-producing hub, the city features a unique grid layout and wide boulevards. Los Mochis is one of Mexico's most productive agricultural centers, famous for its fertile soil and high-quality produce. It is the starting point for the 'Chepe Express' train, which climbs into the Sierra Madre. Nearby, the port of Topolobampo offers beautiful bays, seafood, and boat trips to see the 'Pechocho' dolphin. With its high-end dining specializing in Sinaloan seafood, its clean urban design, and its strategic position for adventure tourism, Los Mochis is a sophisticated and energetic northern city."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Ausgangspunkt des berühmten Kupfer-Canyon-Zuges El Chepe.", "Gegründet von dem amerikanischen Stadtplaner Albert K. Owen im 19. Jahrhundert.", "Bekannt für den Parque Sinaloa, einen großen botanischen Garten mitten in der Stadt."],
      hu: [],
      ro: [],
      en: ["Starting point for the Chepe Express, which travels 350+ kilometers to Creel.", "Home to the Sinaloa Park and Botanical Garden with 10+ hectares.", "Topolobampo Bay is only 20 kilometers from the city center.", "The city was founded in 1903 as a planned company town.", "The Benjamin Johnston Botanical Garden features plants from across 5 continents.", "Located at an altitude of only 10 meters above sea level.", "One of the top national producers of high-quality sugarcane and grains.", "Average annual temperature is a tropical 25 degrees Celsius."]
    }
